Gather the ingredients.

Place @raisins{2%ounces} and @prunes{4%ounces} into a small bowl and pour over enough water to cover. Add @lemon juice{1%tablespoon} and let soak for at least ~{60%minutes}. Drain. Roughly chop the prunes.

Meanwhile, heat @butter{1%ounce} in a large #pan{}. Add @onion{1}(chopped) and cook for ~{5%minutes}. Add @lamb{1%pound}(boneless, trimmed and cut into 1/2-inch cubes), @ground lamb{8%ounces}, and @garlic{2%cloves}(crushed). Fry for ~{5%minutes}, stirring constantly until browned.

Pour @lamb stock{2/3%cup} into the pan. Bring to a boil, then lower the heat, cover, and simmer for ~{60%minutes}, or until the lamb is tender.

Add the remaining stock and bring to a boil. Add @rice{2%cups}(long-grain white, rinsed and drained) and a large pinch of @saffron{}. Stir, then cover, and simmer for ~{15%minutes}, or until the rice is tender.

Add the drained @raisins{} and drained chopped @prunes{}, and @salt{} and @pepper{} to taste. Heat through for a few minutes, then turn out onto a warmed serving dish and garnish with sprigs of @parsley{}(flat-leaf).